            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0256" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3777: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-01T01:00:00+08:00">February 1, 1932—1
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 31—2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Japanese Consul General has just informed me that the Chinese has [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">have</hi>] begun attack on the Japanese positions.
                    Chinese Mayor <pb facs="0257" n="153" xml:id="pg153"/> reports that Japanese
                    started attacking at 11:30. Truce no longer obtains. Rush supplemental naval
                    forces.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
